.\" Distro-authored man page for the Fedora pidp8i package.
.\" Candidate for upstreaming to the PiDP-8/I project.
.TH D8TAPE 1 "November 21, 2026" "PiDP-8/I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
d8tape \- disassemble and convert DECtape (paper tape) images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B d8tape
.RI [ options ]
.I papertapefile
.RI [ papertapefile ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B d8tape
dumps the RIM- or BIN-formatted DECtape/paper-tape files named on the
command line, disassembling them for reading. With
.B \-r
and/or
.B \-b
it also writes RIM and/or BIN reformatted copies, named after the input
with
.I .rim
or
.I .bin
appended.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-b
generate a BIN-formatted output (adds
.IR .bin )
.TP
.B \-d
suppress disassembly (conversion-only mode)
.TP
.B \-r
generate a RIM-formatted output (adds
.IR .rim )
.TP
.B \-v
verbose operation
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ptp2txt (1),
.BR palbart (1)
